Subject: Council Poll: Axon Technology Briefing Availability


Good afternoon, City Council (Bcc=92d),


The Police Department is exploring additional technology solutions availabl=
e through Axon that could support the City=92s public safety operations. As=
 part of that exploration, Axon has offered to provide Council members with=
 an IN PERSON informational briefing and demonstration of its technology.


The briefing will focus primarily on Axon=92s Automated License Plate Recog=
nition (ALPR) technology, including its Outpost fixed license plate reader =
and video solution. Axon will also provide an overview of other public safe=
ty technology, including Dedrone airspace security, as well as information =
regarding data security and privacy, ethical oversight, potential contract =
scope, and financial considerations.


The purpose of this briefing is informational only. It is intended to provi=
de Council members with an opportunity to learn more about the technology a=
nd ask questions directly of Axon representatives. Participation does not r=
epresent a commitment by the City to purchase or implement any particular p=
roduct.


To accommodate Council schedules and allow for a more conversational presen=
tation and Q&A, Axon has proposed several identical one-hour small-group se=
ssions (maximum of two Council Members per session).


Please reply to me at your earliest opportunity and indicate ALL of the tim=
e slots below that you would be available to attend. We will use the respon=
ses to coordinate the sessions.


Tuesday, August 25:

  *   1:00=962:00 p.m.
  *   2:00=963:00 p.m.
  *   3:00=964:00 p.m.
  *   4:00=965:00 p.m.


Tuesday, September 1:

  *   1:00=962:00 p.m.
  *   2:00=963:00 p.m.
  *   3:00=964:00 p.m.
  *   4:00=965:00 p.m.


Thank you, and please let me know if you have any questions.


Best wishes,

Martin



